        <p>Mn Daaa Hauls, Coloured straws ans getting • 11 Do chic Parieiennes prefer hate of straw, or fleecy hate of milk munlin mounted on wire. They are trimmed with pale t•ffetws and aigrette. of beautifully made flower.. A wire hat, with wide brim, is covered with pale pink toilet., over which in laid frilled plink chiffon of • sfill paler pink. The °town is edged with • fleecy frill of the chiffon. On the left is an aigrette bunch of ehaded pink roses, mixed with Parma violets nod secured by • diamond buckle. The broad brim in turned up at the back with *bouquet of violet. and • pink satin bow, held by dianiond</p>
        <p>it. E.ghon.</p>
        <p>Quaintly suggestive of Ws be a bonnet that is noniing into fashion for young ladies, with ito square, flat rim, trimmings of white gauze ribbon and feather., a gauze ribbon marl being tied in n bow to hang with the ends at one ode in a truly picturesque fashion. A little spring coat with a battlement collar is made in soft sago green serge, and the collar is edged with t tiny line of iyory• I inted guipure, and then bordered with a narrow killing of satin.</p>
        <p>A design suitable to a schoolroom maiden is rd purple mohair, with black xtriek and belt, fastening with plain gold buttons, and showing an under bodice of purple silk. To middle.s.ged ladies • basqued blouse is soine, tun. more becoming than a handed one, and a charming model of this type is of dark green and white striped glace, made with a short, box pleated basque, beaded by • fold of dark green velvet. There is a eimulated yoke formed id alternate stripes of dark green ribbon-velvet and yellow lane insertion running Strom the shoulders. A full jabot of yellow I.e reaches nearly to the waiet, and the sleeves are etriped from shoulder puff to wrist with love inurtion and velvsbribbon.</p>
        <p>A charming model coat for Wearing over shirts Sod bloame is of tan,oloursd fated cloth, and this to handsomely brstded round tin edges sod on the riven and naffs.</p>
        <p>The prettiest belm -- and the belt is enjoying unusual prominenis just now --are those of white leather with turiiimise and gold clasp.. A new mid rather orn•te chin, but absolutely eimply cod shirt-114e in not, emetic of white open work embroidery, worn with plain narrow turn over oilier end oravat, and soft to emtch. Any of toy readers who have • pretty piece of Madeira work lying idle in • drawer, or a demod4 embroidered weithing gown, may well hehion theniselvee • shirt of the sort.</p>
        <p>... , ..... Sash.. of chiffon are being tremendously need for gowns on the French stage. Ati entree. who forms oise of the Jane Nlay troupe wore in one piece • charming evening gown of pale maize brocade. with chiffon trimmed bodioe, the skirt having chiffon ecarves sheding from maize to • deeper yellow at intervals running the length of her skirt, and !maenad down negligently at the hem' so that they do not float 100 n... Black grenadine over colour is much in vogue lon the more itreasy cless of bolero cape., • charming epecionen Les for foundation • shot ofone in green and heliotrope, which in plainly nettle through the traneparent grenaline The bolero at edged with • band of jet pueeinentene. and in front there le • c.o.d. of yellow leas, while the sleeves, which reach to the elbow, are formed of alternating frills of this lace and of black chiffon. Another motel hes the aware of black jetted paseenwntena over white satin, edged with }rine of accordion crepe-de•chine, which is alai um.' for the oleeves; while • third ernart wrap is of richly ".welled' ecru Inc.. bright with emeraide, amethysta, and gold beads, laced over Mack MOM The sleeve. of this latter cape are of kilted chiffon, which has narrow satin ribbon run along the edge.</p>
