        <p>Witir-onno in, •lonee OH other Whitalustido Conferroces aessorke of the year, the time for</p>
        <p>-------- mid Conferences, and during the present week there has been a Congrem of co-operatorn at Perth mel con ference• of the ' various Friendly Societien in different parts of the country at which matter!, of intufogt to a very large portion f the ennonimity have bean due come&amp; Mr. W. tfct th, the chairman of the Scottish Co epee alive Wroliwile Society, filled the chair st the Perth Col:grius and hia presidential address was Instinct with northern energy and shrewdnem. It contained ore anggeetion which will tel doubt be the subject of II great deal if con- , sidoration ill the immediate future. This wan the : pri ivies! that io-operators shinill, as co-operntors, begin to take All active partici politics. /fa holds Of) to his colleagues iii the co-operative move- ment the im•rnple of the trades tinenliate and the advocates of temperance. These have powerholly influenced the legialation of ffu country, but, as I 0 points alit, they li.uo nly done this by the lavish etperiditure of time, energy and money, end by the display of un- limited peraisterice and tenacity. As the co- operator. now if. n busineas of ribout • year sod a• there is estimated to be nearly one- ementh rff the whole populatitin of the country in- tstacJ directly er indirectly 111 ca.-operation it can hardly be questioned that they could very candy male, their influent.ee felt both in lolal mei mnup.ri.l politica, if they were so minded. Itut are they so Are they prepwed to act as aeoperators hrst nod a. Liberals or Torien. Itadienle f/T Socialists alter- wards- It luay seriously be doubted whether U..., queetiens will be answered in the affirma- tive. Mr. Mal wistt's speech has no double beau :largely shaped by the peculiar position of affairs With regard to ci.eijeratem ii. Scetlarel just POW. %eel...teen are at the present ; time in onse pert. of Soff land enjoying the I [amity of • real downright boycott on the part !other tradminen,and imperially the butchery. The butchers of 